# Line endings, enforced in the repository rather than left to each clone.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. `.editorconfig` has said `end_of_line = lf` since Phase 0,
# and IDE0055 enforces it at build time under EnforceCodeStyleInBuild — but
# `.editorconfig` describes what the file should contain, and nothing was making
# a checkout produce it. Git for Windows defaults to `core.autocrlf=true`, so a
# clone there rewrites every text file to CRLF on checkout. The index stays LF,
# CI checks out on Linux and stays LF, and the repository looks consistent from
# everywhere except the machine where it is not.
#
# That is where the published image broke: `docker build` sends the WORKING
# TREE, so a Windows checkout hands the compiler CRLF sources while the same
# commit builds clean in CI. A formatting rule the build enforces, a working
# tree nothing normalised, and a gate that only ever ran on Linux (§13.68).
#
# `text=auto` lets Git detect binary files and leave them alone; `eol=lf` makes
# the working tree LF on every platform, not just in the index. Existing Windows
# checkouts need one re-normalisation to pick this up — the README says how.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, named rather than detected, because a false positive here corrupts
# the file rather than merely annoying someone.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
